    "body": "I think the non-normative description (aimed at web developers) should definitely mention it can be rejected.\r\n\r\nThe normative description I'm less clear on. As per https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#algorithm-control-flow modern practice is to not state something can rethrow, but I do remember @domenic not being entirely comfortable with relying on the Web IDL layer for wrapping a thrown exception into a rejected promise return value. I don't think we ever settled on guidance for it though.",
